course: dictionary
lesson: 1552
title: Champion: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word champion can change its meaning depending on the words around it. You can work out which meaning is right by reading the clues in the sentence. Ask yourself: who or what is being talked about, and what is happening?
explain: «Theo's mum has been the family champion at a board game for six years.» Here a champion is the person who has won the most games. The clue is at a board game for six years, which tells you she keeps winning.
explain: «A champion of children's rights» uses champion in a different way. A champion of something is a person who fights for it and speaks up for it. The clue is rights, which is a cause, not a prize.
explain: To champion something is a verb, so it is something you do: you support it and argue for it strongly. «Champion!» said on its own, as in UK informal talk, means excellent or great. Check the sentence to see which meaning fits.
fact: A champion is a person or team that has won a competition, especially the most important one.
fact: A champion of something is a person who fights for it or speaks up for it.
fact: To champion something means to support it and argue for it strongly, as in «champion recycling».
fact: «Champion!» (UK, informal, old-fashioned) means excellent or great.
fact: A championship is a competition held to decide the title, such as a league or a cup. Words like «world champion», «reigning champion» and «Olympic champion» are common in sport.
exercise: «Theo's mum has been the family champion at a board game for six years.» What does champion mean here? | *A person who has won the most games, the best player | A person who makes board games | A person who loses every game | A rule book for the game
exercise: The news says «an AI beat a world champion at the board game Go». What is a world champion? | A robot that plays board games | A player who has never played before | A player who came last in the contest | *The best player in the world at that game, who won the top competition
exercise: «Mountain animals are champions of cold and thin air.» What does champions mean here? | Animals who are often cold | *Experts who cope very well with the cold and thin air | People who climb mountains to help the animals | Winners of a race up the mountain
test: What does it mean to champion a cause, such as recycling? | To win a prize for it | To put it in a cupboard | *To support it and argue for it strongly | To ignore it completely
test: Which word means a competition held to decide the title? | *championship | champion | champions only | championing
exam: A friend says «Champion!» after you pass a tough test. What does it mean? | A type of cup | A knight in an old story | *Excellent, great | Something that wins a prize
